• **Version-claim markers:** no `0.24` markers remain. Each moved marker has its paragraph re-read with citations to the 0.25.2 source. Where the claim changed (cancel error spellings, the new per-run hook that sees a sub-agent's task, the new Rate limited error text), the old sentence is kept and marked superseded. It was not a bulk find-and-replace.
• **Docs:** the CHANGELOG has the 0.25.2 line, and CLAUDE.md changed only at its one marker.
• Binary: target/debug/yoyo --version runs. I did not re-run the test suite, since the harness had already passed it.

One behaviour change to know about: the existing test opt_in_every_attempt_dying_after_text_terminates_nonzero_within_the_cap in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs was changed to match the new behaviour. With retry_after_partial turned on, the worst case went from 6 requests to 24. yoagent now retries 4 times inside each of yoyo's 6 attempts, because 0.25.2 classifies an overloaded error as a rate limit. Stderr also now shows "Rate limited" instead of the provider's own "Overloaded" message. The edit is recorded in the test as a superseded reading, and with the setting off (the default) the rows still show 1 request. This repo's .yoyo.toml turns the setting on, so the evolve loop gets the 24-request worst case.

